<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia Budget-Revenue measures summary.</title>
<headline>Australia Budget-Revenue measures summary.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>This is a summary of revenue measures announced by Treasurer Peter Costello in his Tuesday budget for the year to June 30, 1998.</p>
<p>The impact of each measure on the coming four fiscal years is shown, in A$ millions, and the measures are ordered approximately by size.</p>
<p>				   1997/98   1998/99   1999/00   2000/01</p>
<p>TOTAL REVENUE MEASURES  </p>
<p>					  71	 391     -1,006   -1,758</p>
<p>TAX REBATE ON SAVINGS. Tax concessions for savings, with costs to revenue that offset lower spending from the abolition of the planned government contribution to retirement savings.</p>
<p>					   -	-350     -1,370   -2,040</p>
<p>SUPERANNUATION PRESERVATION. Detail policy change.  </p>
<p>					   -	   -	  -35     -105</p>
<p>OTHER SUPERANNUATION MEASURES</p>
<p>					 -24	 -50	  -26	-22</p>
<p>TAX CRACKDOWN. On income injected into loss-making trusts.</p>
<p>					   5	  15	   20	 20</p>
<p>TAX CRACKDOWN. On company profits disguised as loans.  </p>
<p>					   2	  50	   30	 30</p>
<p>TAX CRACKDOWN. On foreign-sourced income.</p>
<p>					   -	 150	  150	150</p>
<p>NATIONAL CRIME AUTHORITY INVESTIGATIONS. Of &quot;complex money-laundering and tax evasion schemes.&quot;</p>
<p>					   -	  40	   40	  -</p>
<p>MISCELLANEOUS</p>
<p>					  88	 536	  185	209</p>
</text>
